# The own body never blocks the view (#385.9, #451): looking down 30, 60 and 85 degrees the body sits on a neck
# pivot pushed back behind the eyes, the faces within the clearance of an eye are hidden, the legs stay drawn.
# status.json (PROPOSED names, 385.9 implements them; units = engine units):
#   vr.body.push              the push-back along the facing now (units, > 0)
#   vr.body.neckPivot         the neck pivot (object x y z)
#   vr.body.nearestBodyToEye  the nearest DRAWN body vertex to either eye (units); must stay beyond the clearance
#   vr.body.clearance         the clearance (units; cfg default 15)
#   vr.body.hiddenNearEye     the faces hidden by the near-eye rule this frame (>= 0; > 0 looking down)
#   vr.body.legsDrawn         true while faces below keepBelow are still drawn
# The sim's head pitch is the 2nd angle of `vr-sim head rot <yaw> <pitch> <roll>`: + looks up, so down is negative.
# Captures go to the evidence folder (%LOCALAPPDATA%\ArxFatalisVR\evidence\385.9\), never into git.
#   .\scripts\dev\xrs-run.ps1 body-look-down
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -VrSim idle -Sequence body-look-down -Save mvp-new-game
@sim idle
@save mvp-new-game
@args --loadslot 0

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
@assert vr.body.bound eq true
@assert vr.body.active eq true
@assert vr.body.clearance gt 0
@remember clearance vr.body.clearance

# Looking ahead: the push is there, the body is drawn
vr-sim head rot 0 0 0
@frames 15
@assert vr.body.push gt 0
@assert vr.body.hiddenNearEye ge 0
@assert vr.body.legsDrawn eq true
@shot ahead

# 30 degrees down
vr-sim head rot 0 -30 0
@frames 15
@assert vr.body.push gt 0
@assert vr.body.nearestBodyToEye gt {clearance}
@assert vr.body.hiddenNearEye ge 0
@assert vr.body.legsDrawn eq true
@shot down-30

# 60 degrees down
vr-sim head rot 0 -60 0
@frames 15
@assert vr.body.push gt 0
@assert vr.body.nearestBodyToEye gt {clearance}
@assert vr.body.hiddenNearEye ge 0
@assert vr.body.legsDrawn eq true
@shot down-60

# 85 degrees down: the torso is right under the eyes - faces are hidden, none is within the clearance, the legs stay
vr-sim head rot 0 -85 0
@frames 15
@assert vr.body.push gt 0
@assert vr.body.nearestBodyToEye gt {clearance}
@assert vr.body.hiddenNearEye ge 0
@assert vr.body.legsDrawn eq true
@shot down-85

# Back up: nothing is left hidden by the rule beyond what the pose needs, the body is still drawn
vr-sim head rot 0 0 0
@frames 15
@assert vr.body.legsDrawn eq true
@assert vr.body.nearestBodyToEye gt {clearance}

@assert errors eq 0
